1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,739
What if someone closed the Strait of Gibraltar tomorrow?

2
00:00:04,239 --> 00:00:09,795
It's only about 13 kilometers wide, but it keeps the Mediterranean alive.

3
00:00:10,215 --> 00:00:14,394
The sea loses more water to evaporation than its rivers bring in.

4
00:00:14,814 --> 00:00:19,349
Cut off from the Atlantic, its level would fall by up to 1 meter every year.

5
00:00:19,799 --> 00:00:22,938
In about 1,000 years, most of it would be gone.

6
00:00:23,438 --> 00:00:26,453
A salt desert, kilometers below sea level.

7
00:00:26,953 --> 00:00:31,993
And this isn't just a thought experiment. It happened, about six million years ago.

8
00:00:32,493 --> 00:00:38,256
Then the Atlantic broke back through, in what may have been the biggest flood in Earth's history.

9
00:00:38,656 --> 00:00:42,306
Refilling most of the sea in as little as two years.

10
00:00:42,856 --> 00:00:45,442
Would you walk across the dry Mediterranean?
